      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Three Runtime Signals",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Symptom",
            "Cause"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`TypeError: unhashable type: 'list'`",
              "list arg into lru_cache"
            ],
            [
              "`RuntimeWarning: coroutine was never awaited`",
              "sync wrapper on async def"
            ],
            [
              "traceback stops at the wrapper",
              "re-raise without `from e`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "except ValueError as e:",
            "    raise RetryError('gave up') from e  # cause"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Debug Toolkit"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`f.__name__`, `f.__doc__`, `f.__wrapped__` first",
            "`inspect.unwrap(f)` walks the whole chain",
            "`f.__closure__[0].cell_contents`",
            "`f.__code__.co_freevars`",
            "`inspect.signature(f)`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Two Definitions To Keep"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Closure = inner function + captured cells, alive after the outer returns",
            "Capture is by reference, never a snapshot",
            "Decorator = callable taking a function, returning a replacement",
            "`@d` above `def f` is exactly `f = d(f)`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Template To Memorise",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "def deco(fn):",
            "    @wraps(fn)",
            "    def wrapper(*a, **kw):",
            "        return fn(*a, **kw)",
            "    return wrapper"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Always `@functools.wraps(fn)`",
            "Always forward `*args, **kwargs`",
            "Always `return` the call's result",
            "Bottom decorator wraps first; top one runs first"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Stdlib By Heart"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Name",
            "Use"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`wraps` / `update_wrapper`",
              "keep identity"
            ],
            [
              "`partial`",
              "pre-bind args"
            ],
            [
              "`cache` / `lru_cache`",
              "memoise"
            ],
            [
              "`cached_property`",
              "per-instance value"
            ],
            [
              "`singledispatch` / `total_ordering`",
              "dispatch, ordering"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Choosing And Typing"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Class-based when you need named per-function state",
            "Add `__get__` if that class decorates methods",
            "Use `ParamSpec` so typed callers keep their signatures"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
