    {
      "page_title": "The Two Canonical Examples",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. The Closure Everyone Learns",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "def make_adder(n):",
            "    def add(x):",
            "        return x + n",
            "    return add",
            "",
            "add5 = make_adder(5)",
            "print(add5(3))  # 8"
          ],
          "runnable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`make_adder` is a factory, not an adder",
            "Each call builds a fresh `add` function",
            "`n` outlives `make_adder` inside a cell",
            "`add5(3) == 8` because `n` is still 5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Inspect That Cell"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Expression",
            "Value"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`add5.__name__`",
              "`'add'`"
            ],
            [
              "`add5.__code__.co_freevars`",
              "`('n',)`"
            ],
            [
              "`add5.__closure__[0].cell_contents`",
              "`5`"
            ],
            [
              "`make_adder(9)(3)`",
              "`12`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Two adders never share one cell",
            "`make_adder(2) is not make_adder(2)`",
            "Same shape powers every decorator factory"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "9. Factory: Three Nested Layers",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "def repeat(n):",
            "    def deco(fn):",
            "        @wraps(fn)",
            "        def w(*a, **kw):",
            "            for _ in range(n):",
            "                r = fn(*a, **kw)",
            "            return r",
            "        return w",
            "    return deco"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Layer",
            "Takes"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`repeat`",
              "config `n`"
            ],
            [
              "`deco`",
              "the function"
            ],
            [
              "`w`",
              "call args"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "10. Reading The Layers"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`n` is captured once, at decoration time",
            "`w` closes over both `fn` and `n`",
            "`r` holds the last call's return value",
            "`@wraps(fn)` keeps name, doc, `__wrapped__`",
            "Usage is `@repeat(3)`, parens included"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@repeat(3)",
            "def ping():",
            "    print('pong')"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "One Rule, Two Shapes",
          "text": "A plain decorator takes a function and returns a replacement. A decorator factory takes configuration and returns that plain decorator. Nothing else changes."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Missing Parens & Real Frameworks",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "11. The Missing-Parens Bug",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@repeat  # wrong: no parens",
            "def ping():",
            "    print('pong')"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`@repeat` passes the *function* as `n`",
            "`repeat(ping)` returns `deco`, not a wrapper",
            "`ping` is now bound to `deco` itself",
            "Decoration succeeds; nothing raises yet"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "12. Why The Error Travels"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Stage",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "import time",
              "silent, no error"
            ],
            [
              "`ping()`",
              "wants a function arg"
            ],
            [
              "message",
              "`missing 1 required`"
            ],
            [
              "blame lands on",
              "the call site"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Cause is the decorator line, not the call",
            "`range(n)` never runs, so `n` looks innocent",
            "Check `ping.__name__` — it reads `'deco'`",
            "Fix: write `@repeat(3)`, with parens"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "13. Guard The Factory"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "def repeat(n):",
            "    if callable(n):",
            "        raise TypeError('use @repeat(k)')"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "14. Factories You Already Use",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Library",
            "Decorator"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Flask",
              "`@app.route('/')`"
            ],
            [
              "pytest",
              "`@fixture`"
            ],
            [
              "Django",
              "`@login_required`"
            ],
            [
              "Click",
              "`@click.command()`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Flask's `@app.route` takes a URL, then wraps",
            "pytest's `@fixture` works bare or configured",
            "`@login_required` is plain: no config needed",
            "Click's `@click.command()` builds a command"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "15. Parens Or No Parens"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Form",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`@deco`",
              "plain decorator"
            ],
            [
              "`@deco()`",
              "factory, defaults"
            ],
            [
              "`@deco(3)`",
              "factory, configured"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Read the docs once; memorise the shape",
            "Bare-or-called factories accept both, deliberately",
            "When unsure, print `f.__name__` after import"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "The Habit Worth Keeping",
          "text": "If a decorator takes any configuration, it is a factory and needs parens. A wrong bare `@repeat` fails far from its cause, so check the decorator line first."
        }
      ]
    }
